    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d710a-103">

                <pb facs="0568" n="382" xml:id="pg382"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Truman Papers</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">United States Delegation Working Paper</hi></head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Potsdam</placeName>, <date
                        ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-chapter-heading" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1945-07-25T11:00:00+03:00">July 25, 1945, 11 a.m.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Agenda for the Meeting of Heads
                        of Governments, July</hi> 25, 1945</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Polish Western Frontier<anchor n="3" xml:id="d710a-103-f1"/></item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Disposition of German Fleet and Merchant Marine<anchor n="4"
                            xml:id="d710a-103-f2"/></item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>German Reparations</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>Transfer of populations from Poland &amp; Czechoslovakia<anchor n="5"
                            xml:id="d710a-103-f3"/></item>
                    <label>[5.]</label>
                    <item>Waterways<anchor n="6" xml:id="d710a-103-f4"/></item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d710a-103-f1" n="3" xml:id="d710a-103-f1-content">
                <p>Opposite this item is the following marginal manuscript notation by Dunn: “Eden
                    opposed to discussing this morning”.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d710a-103-f2" n="4" xml:id="d710a-103-f2-content">
                <p>Items 2 and 3 are bracketed together with the following marginal manuscript
                    notation by Dunn: “Br[itish] ask to postpone”.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d710a-103-f3" n="5" xml:id="d710a-103-f3-content">
                <p>Item 4 was added in manuscript by Dunn with the following marginal notation:
                    “British will ask to add to agenda.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d710a-103-f4" n="6" xml:id="d710a-103-f4-content">
                <p>The last item was added in manuscript by Truman.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
